instanceFunctions.endAnimation:
Forciblly ends this Character's current animation. Acts as if there were no more animation keyframes after the frame this function is ran.

Any framescript code that plays on the first frame of the next animation will execute before any code after this function call will execute. This applies both when this function is called in a framescript keyframe and in the Character's main script.

```haxe
// NOTES:
// "self" refers to the fighter running this code.
// These are set on the same fighter animation.

// frame 1
Engine.log("Starting animation 1.");
Engine.log("Starting animation 2.");
Engine.log("Starting animation 3.");

// frame 10
Engine.log("Ending animation.");
self.endAnimation();
Engine.log("Finished ending animation 1.");
Engine.log("Finished ending animation 2.");
Engine.log("Finished ending animation 3.");
```

Output:
```
Starting animation 1.
Starting animation 2.
Starting animation 3.
Ending animation.
Starting animation 1.
Starting animation 2.
Starting animation 3.
Finished ending animation 1.
Finished ending animation 2.
Finished ending animation 3.
```

instanceFunctions.updateCharacterStats:
Updates this character's [CharacterStats](CharacterStats.md).

Parameters:
- The new values for each [CharacterStats](CharacterStats.md) in an object. You only have to include the stats you want to modify.

```haxe
// Sets the number of airdashes this character can perform to 5.
// "self" refers to the character that will be affected.
self.updateCharacterStats({
	airdashLimit: 5
});
